A named slot with an argument, forwarded down a recursion, on every target.

`frame` is a member of its own cycle, so it is built at run time everywhere.
Each level inserts `label(n)`, and the level below populates its own `label`
by forwarding to the one it was handed, so every level renders the caller's
population with its own `n`. On html, fyne and gtk4 the caller's population is
spliced into a copy of `frame`, and the copy's recursive site is handed
content cloned from the same statements with the same shape -- so it reuses the
copy rather than copying without end. bubbletea and android pass the slot as a
function and the recursion composes them at run time.

The population also calls `describe(d)`, which reads the window's state.
Lifted whole into a prop, as a call is when it reads nothing the population
binds, its argument would name `d` at the site, where nothing binds it -- so
it stays in the copy. And it is the only call of `describe`, so the shake that
walked no population dropped the declaration and left the call naming nothing.

Two more defects closed here, each visible in the output. A slot insertion's
arguments were shared between a declaration and its clone, so renaming one
copy's props repointed the template's -- the second copy of `frame` read the
first copy's `n`, which fyne and gtk4 spelled as a bare `n` their records do not
declare. And the optimizer's clone of a node shared its populations, so a
substitution into a clone wrote the caller's content into `frame`'s own
recursive population: bubbletea rendered the top level's content at every
level.

deny out/go/fyne/model.go `describe\(n\)` -- a copy reads its prop through its cell; a bare `n` is a constructor argument, and in the second copy not even that
deny out/go/gtk4/model.go `describe\(n\)` -- as above, for the gtk4 record
deny out/go/bubbletea/model.go `(?s)"level ".*"level "` -- the caller's population is written once, in the closure the view passes; the recursion forwards the slot it was handed
deny out/kotlin/android/app/src/main/java/test/sngl/app/MainScreen.kt `(?s)"level ".*"level "` -- as above, for the composable
-- app.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"

output {
    go {
        bubbletea
        fyne
        gtk4
    }
    kotlin {
        android
    }
    none {
        html
    }
}

component frame(n int, label component(depth int) node) node {
    vbox {
        label(n)
        if n > 0 {
            frame(n=n - 1) {
                component label(d) {
                    label(d)
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

window {
    var depth = 2
    var mark = "*"

    func describe(d int) => "{d}{mark}"

    vbox {
        button(text="deeper", @click { depth = depth + 1 })
        frame(n=depth) {
            component label(d) {
                text(value="level {describe(d)} of {depth}")
            }
        }
    }
}
